paperweight-skel (0.2.66-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Replace the broken waybar power button with wlogout: the old
    paperweight-power wofi menu lived in ~/.local/bin, which is never on
    PATH for waybar/sway-spawned processes, so it silently did nothing.
    wlogout ships as a real /usr/bin binary and renders a themed row of
    icon buttons (lock/logout/suspend/restart/shutdown), matching the
    XFCE-style Ctrl+Alt+Delete session dialog. Bound to both the waybar
    power button and new Ctrl+Alt+Delete / Ctrl+Alt+BackSpace sway
    keybindings (BackSpace covers Chromebook keyboards, which have no
    dedicated Delete key).
  * wlogout/layout: fixed "Invalid JSON Data" hang on open — wlogout's
    config parser expects a bare sequence of concatenated JSON objects,
    not a JSON array; the file was wrapped in [ ... ] with commas, which
    is valid JSON generally but not what wlogout's own parser accepts.
  * wlogout is now the 8th per-user theme file, wired into
    paperweight-theme (~/.config/wlogout/{layout,style.css,themes/}) —
    see THEME-AUTHORING.md.
  * wlogout/themes/*.css: buttons were stretching to fill the full screen
    height (single row, and GTK3 CSS has no height/width/max-height
    property to cap it). Shrunk via a tall top/bottom margin instead —
    the only sizing lever GTK3 CSS actually supports for a fill-expanded
    widget.
  * Fix the same ~/.local/bin PATH bug for paperweight-network ($mod+n)
    and paperweight-volume (media keys) by moving both to /usr/bin,
    following the precedent already set for paperweight-theme (0.2.53).
  * debian/postinst: chmod +x list and upgrade-path cleanup/propagation
    updated to match — stale ~/.local/bin copies of paperweight-power,
    paperweight-network, and paperweight-volume are removed on upgrade;
    ~/.config/wlogout/ is populated for existing users.

